Package: uplink-watchdog
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: curl, iputils-ping, iproute2, ifupdown, systemd, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0
Description: primary uplink watchdog with webservice-controlled backup
 uplink-watchdog checks the primary uplink (eth0) on layer 3 by pinging
 public targets through it. After it has been down continuously for
 FAILOVER_AFTER seconds (default 300), the backup interface (any ifupdown
 interface, default wwan0) is brought up just long enough to notify a
 webservice, then polled every POLL_INTERVAL seconds to ask it what to do.
 On the answer "vpn" a configurable command runs and the backup stays up.
 Normal traffic is never rerouted. As soon as the primary answers again,
 the VPN is stopped, the webservice is told and the backup goes down.
 .
 Options are in /etc/default/uplink-watchdog.
